Kandor - patch 7: the AGDC fix for Navi (AMDRadeonX6000Framebuffer) as a Lilu patch
Apply after patches 1-6 (see README.md). Author: ne1rom, with assistance from Claude (Anthropic)
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

On Tahoe, OCLP installs the Monterey AMDRadeonX6000Framebuffer 4.8.101 for Navi on Macs without AVX2. Like
AMDSupport 4.0.8, it accepts only the 16-entry AGDC structures, so displaypolicyd never brings a Navi eGPU
display online. Four find/replace pairs, each matching exactly once in OCLP 3.0.0-rc.5's framebuffer
(md5 1fe8bd73e886e669c3280be2ec6bc779) and zero times in Apple's own Tahoe framebuffer. Tahoe (kernel 25) and
later only, krygpu=AMD; shares the -krynoagdc switch with patch 4.

Tested as a Lilu patch on Tahoe 26.7.3 / OCLP 3.0.0-rc.5 with an RX 6900 XT (Navi 21), with a build that used a
kernel 22+ gate (on Tahoe the code path is the same as with this kernel 25+ gate): with it displaypolicyd
reports "Do online device ... completed" (4K@60); with -krynoagdc the eGPU displays stay dark and displaypolicyd
reports "not completed ... err 3:3:0:0:0".

